.TH PATMAN 1 "October 2026" "patman 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
patman \- create, check and email patch series with Patchwork integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patman
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Patman helps you create, send, track and review patch series for projects
that take patches by email, such as U-Boot and the Linux kernel.
.PP
It creates patches from a git branch, cleans them up by removing unwanted
tags, inserts a cover letter with change logs, runs the patches through
checkpatch and its own checks, and emails them out with
.B git send-email
or, where there is no working SMTP, through a web relay.  It can also track
a series on Patchwork and gather review tags into the commits.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send
Format, check and email the patches.  This is the default command.
.TP
.B series
Manage local series and follow their Patchwork status across versions.
.TP
.B patchwork
Manage the connection to a Patchwork server.
.TP
.B review
AI-review a Patchwork series and store or send the result.
.TP
.B status
Show the Patchwork status of a series and gather its review tags.
.TP
.B upstream
Manage the upstream trees that series are sent to.
.PP
Run
.BI "patman " command " \-\-help"
for the options of a particular command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .patman
Per-repository configuration at the top of the git tree.  It overrides
.B ~/.patman
(the user's global configuration) which in turn overrides the project's
tracked
.BR .patman-defaults .
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation is published at
.UR https://patman.readthedocs.io/
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Patman was written by Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org> and contributors.
